  "title": "Nancy Kassebaum Baker, former US senator from Kansas, passes away at 94",
  "summary": "Nancy Kassebaum Baker, a Kansas governor's daughter who became the first woman elected to the US Senate without following a spouse into office, has died. She was 94. She loved Kansas and represented it for 18 years in the US Senate. Her modest demeanor and progressive Republican ideals endeared her to voters.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Nancy Kassebaum Baker, a Kansas governor's daughter, became the first woman elected to the US Senate without following a spouse into office.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "She was 94 and died on Friday of natural causes according to her son, Bill Kassebaum.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "She served three terms in the US Senate and represented Kansas.",
